{
	"_note": "Sayo keeps the Yorozu Store (the house with the noren south-east of the road): sweeps in front before opening, stands at the counter (the store map's keeper spot) 9:00-17:00, so talking to her there opens the shop (data/shops.json keeper), and takes an offering to the shrine in the evening. She lives in the rooms behind the store (data/maps/sayo_house.json, the side door), where she is before opening, 17:00-18:30 and after the shrine until 21:00, when she goes to bed (away). Sundays the store is shut: she walks over to Grandma Tome's, waits by the house and has tea with her inside after lunch. On her birthday (unless a Sunday) she shuts the store at 12:30, has lunch at Tome's, and spends the afternoon in her rooms before the shrine. Rain or shine the shop opens. Married to the farmer (married_sayo, data/marriage.json) she lives at the farmhouse: by the kotatsu in the second room before 8:30 and from 17:00, the store as before in between, and on a Sunday tea at Tome's 12:40-15:00. Festival days: on Blossom Day the store opens as usual, but she leaves a note on the counter from 13:00 to 15:45 (data/shops.json festival_away) and sits by the picnic mats under the blossoms; on Lantern Night (the store shut) she browses the night food stall from 16:50; on Moon Night she closes at 17:00 and watches the moon from the shrine's gravel from 17:50; at Year's Turn (shut) she stands between the shrine and the bonfire from 18:40. Gifts: fresh summer things, sweets and pretty mine gems; not muddy clay or the bony fish (loach, crucian carp, dace). Dishes: egg and milk ones (tamagoyaki, milk pudding best) and light rice dishes; no river fish on a plate either. Format: README.md, Villagers.",
